IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-notice`

-- ccc18-soira-additional.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 490.04 to 490.07 (additional orders: exemption and variation orders for orders and
-- obligations that began before the amendments came into force, with the appeal and the notices that follow). Part agent ccc18; layer 1. It imports `ccc18-soira-notice`
-- (bands, the end-of-obligation type, helpers). The days on which paragraphs and subsections "come into force" are not stated in the text: where a rule turns on one, the
-- caller states whether the order or obligation began before it. Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE of a type); see the header of `ccc18-soira-notice` and NOTES.md.

§ `Sections 490.04 to 490.07 -- Additional orders`

§ `490.04 Application for exemption order`

-- src:10634 | Additional Orders
-- src:10635 | Application for exemption order
-- src:10636 | 490.04 (1) A person may apply to a court for an order exempting them from
-- src:10637 | (a) an order made under section 490.012 on or after April 15, 2011 but before the day on which this paragraph comes into force; or
-- src:10638 | (b) an obligation under section 490.02901, or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, that began before the day on which this paragraph comes into force.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(1) (src:10634-10638)
GIVEN `(a) the person is subject to an order made under section 490.012 on or after April 15, 2011 but before the day on which paragraph 490.04(1)(a) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the person is subject to an obligation under section 490.02901, or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, that began before the day on which paragraph 490.04(1)(b) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04(1) the person may apply to a court for an exemption order` MEANS
    IF `(a) the person is subject to an order made under section 490.012 on or after April 15, 2011 but before the day on which paragraph 490.04(1)(a) comes into force`
       OR `(b) the person is subject to an obligation under section 490.02901, or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, that began before the day on which paragraph 490.04(1)(b) comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may apply to a court for an order exempting them from (a) an order made under section 490.012 on or after April 15, 2011"

-- src:10639 | Limitation — application
-- src:10640 | (2) A person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b) if, on or after the day on which this subsection comes into force, they have made an application for an exemption order under section 490.02905 or 490.029111 in respect of the same obligation.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(2) (src:10639-10640)
GIVEN `the application is under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on or after the day on which this subsection comes into force, they have made an application for an exemption order under section 490.02905 or 490.029111 in respect of the same obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04(2) the person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the application is under paragraph (1)(b)` AND `on or after the day on which this subsection comes into force, they have made an application for an exemption order under section 490.02905 or 490.029111 in respect of the same obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b) if" they have made such an application

-- src:10641 | Jurisdiction
-- src:10642 | (3) The application shall be made to
-- src:10643 | (a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, if the application is made under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of an order made by such a court; or
-- src:10644 | (b) a court of criminal jurisdiction, in any other case.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(3) (src:10641-10644)
DECLARE `s 490.04(3) court to which the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.04(3)(a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 490.04(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(3) (src:10641-10644)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 490.04(3) court to which the application is made`
`s 490.04(3) the court to which the application shall be made` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` AND `the application is in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    THEN `s 490.04(3)(a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    ELSE `s 490.04(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`   -- "(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction, in any other case"

-- src:10645 | Limitation — exemption order
-- src:10646 | (4) The court shall not make an exemption order in respect of an application made under paragraph (1)(a) if
-- src:10647 | (a) the designated offence that is the basis of the order made under section 490.012 was prosecuted by indictment, the sentence for that offence is a term of imprisonment of two years or more and the victim of that offence was under the age of 18 years; or
-- src:10648 | (b) before or after the order under section 490.012 was made, the person
-- src:10649 | (i) was convicted of a primary offence — or convicted of an offence under section 130 of the National Defence Act in respect of a primary offence — that is not the offence on the basis of which the order was made, or
-- src:10650 | (ii) is or was, as a result of a conviction, subject to another order or obligation under this or another Act of Parliament to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(4) (src:10645-10650)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) the designated offence that is the basis of the order made under section 490.012 was prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) the sentence for that offence is a term of imprisonment of two years or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) the victim of that offence was under the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(i) before or after the order under section 490.012 was made, the person was convicted of a primary offence, or of an offence under section 130 of the National Defence Act in respect of a primary offence, that is not the offence on the basis of which the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(ii) before or after the order was made, the person is or was, as a result of a conviction, subject to another order or obligation under this or another Act of Parliament to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)`
       AND (  (`(a) the designated offence that is the basis of the order made under section 490.012 was prosecuted by indictment` AND `(a) the sentence for that offence is a term of imprisonment of two years or more` AND `(a) the victim of that offence was under the age of 18 years`)
           OR `(b)(i) before or after the order under section 490.012 was made, the person was convicted of a primary offence, or of an offence under section 130 of the National Defence Act in respect of a primary offence, that is not the offence on the basis of which the order was made`
           OR `(b)(ii) before or after the order was made, the person is or was, as a result of a conviction, subject to another order or obligation under this or another Act of Parliament to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court shall not make an exemption order in respect of an application made under paragraph (1)(a) if"

-- src:10651 | Exemption order
-- src:10652 | (5) Subject to subsection (4), the court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that, at the time the order was made or the obligation began,
-- src:10653 | (a) there was no connection between the order or obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act; or
-- src:10654 | (b) the impact of the order or the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, was grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(5) (src:10651-10654)
DECLARE `s 490.04(5) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.04(5) make an exemption order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(5) (src:10651-10654)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that, at the time the order was made or the obligation began, there was no connection between the order or obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that, at the time the order was made or the obligation began, the impact of the order or the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, was grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04(5) the court shall make an exemption order` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that, at the time the order was made or the obligation began, there was no connection between the order or obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
       OR `the court is satisfied that the person has established that, at the time the order was made or the obligation began, the impact of the order or the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, was grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(5) (src:10651-10654)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.04(5) action`
`s 490.04(5) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.04(5) make an exemption order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of a ground and did not make an exemption order"

-- src:10645 | Limitation — exemption order
-- src:10646 | (4) The court shall not make an exemption order in respect of an application made under paragraph (1)(a) if
-- src:10647 | (a) the designated offence that is the basis of the order made under section 490.012 was prosecuted by indictment, the sentence for that offence is a term of imprisonment of two years or more and the victim of that offence was under the age of 18 years; or
-- src:10648 | (b) before or after the order under section 490.012 was made, the person
-- src:10649 | (i) was convicted of a primary offence — or convicted of an offence under section 130 of the National Defence Act in respect of a primary offence — that is not the offence on the basis of which the order was made, or
-- src:10650 | (ii) is or was, as a result of a conviction, subject to another order or obligation under this or another Act of Parliament to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
-- src:10651 | Exemption order
-- src:10652 | (5) Subject to subsection (4), the court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that, at the time the order was made or the obligation began,
-- src:10653 | (a) there was no connection between the order or obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act; or
-- src:10654 | (b) the impact of the order or the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, was grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(4) and (5) (src:10645-10654)
GIVEN `the answer of s 490.04(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 490.04(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04 the court shall make an exemption order, subject to subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 490.04(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall not make an exemption order in respect of an application made under paragraph (1)(a)"
    ELSE `the answer of s 490.04(5)`

-- src:10655 | Factors
-- src:10656 | (6) In determining whether to make the exemption order, the court shall consider
-- src:10657 | (a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the order or obligation;
-- src:10658 | (b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics;
-- src:10659 | (c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim;
-- src:10660 | (d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person;
-- src:10661 | (e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence;
-- src:10662 | (f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person; and
-- src:10663 | (g) any other factors that the court considers relevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(6) (src:10655-10663)
DECLARE `s 490.04(6) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.04(6)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the order or obligation`
    `s 490.04(6)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics`
    `s 490.04(6)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim`
    `s 490.04(6)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person`
    `s 490.04(6)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence`
    `s 490.04(6)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person`
    `s 490.04(6)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant`
    `s 490.04(6) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(6) (src:10655-10663)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether to make the exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 490.04(6) factor`
      `the court considers the matter relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is determining whether to make the exemption order`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining whether to make the exemption order, the court shall consider" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE CONSIDER factor
         WHEN `s 490.04(6)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the order or obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.04(6)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.04(6)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.04(6)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.04(6)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.04(6)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.04(6)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (g): "any other factors that the court considers relevant" is itself in the list
         WHEN `s 490.04(6) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` THEN IF `the court considers the matter relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only factors "that the court considers relevant" are added by paragraph (g)

-- src:10664 | Reasons for decision
-- src:10665 | (7) The court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(7) (src:10664-10665)
DECLARE `s 490.04(7) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.04(7) give reasons for its decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(7) (src:10664-10665)
GIVEN `the court has made a decision under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04(7) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a decision under this section` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "The court shall give reasons for its decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(7) (src:10664-10665)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.04(7) action`
`s 490.04(7) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.04(7) give reasons for its decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not give reasons for its decision"

-- src:10666 | Removal of information from database
-- src:10667 | (8) If the court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(8) (src:10666-10667)
DECLARE `s 490.04(8) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.04(8) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(8) (src:10666-10667)
GIVEN `the court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.04(8) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court makes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.04(8) (src:10666-10667)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.04(8) action`
`s 490.04(8) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.04(8) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made an exemption order and did not order the removal of the information"

§ `490.05 Application for variation order`

-- src:10668 | Application for variation order
-- src:10669 | 490.05 (1) A person may apply to a court for an order to vary the duration of
-- src:10670 | (a) an order made under section 490.012, if the order applies for life under subsection 490.013(2.1), as it read from time to time before the day on which this paragraph comes into force;
-- src:10671 | (b) an obligation under section 490.019, if the obligation applies for life under paragraph 490.022(3)(d) and none of the offences listed in the notice in Form 53 served on the person in respect of the obligation have a maximum term of imprisonment for life;
-- src:10672 | (c) an obligation under section 490.02901, if the obligation applies for life under paragraph 490.02904(3)(d), the obligation began before the day on which this paragraph comes into force and the condition set out in paragraph 490.029051(1)(b) is met; or
-- src:10673 | (d) an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, if the obligation applies for life under subsection 36.2(3) of that Act, the obligation began before the day on which this paragraph comes into force and the condition set out in paragraph 490.029112(1)(b) is met.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(1) (src:10668-10673)
GIVEN `(a) the person is subject to an order made under section 490.012 that applies for life under subsection 490.013(2.1), as it read from time to time before the day on which paragraph 490.05(1)(a) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the person is subject to an obligation under section 490.019 that applies for life under paragraph 490.022(3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) none of the offences listed in the notice in Form 53 served on the person in respect of the obligation have a maximum term of imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) the person is subject to an obligation under section 490.02901 that applies for life under paragraph 490.02904(3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) the obligation began before the day on which paragraph 490.05(1)(c) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) the condition set out in paragraph 490.029051(1)(b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(d) the person is subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act that applies for life under subsection 36.2(3) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(d) the obligation began before the day on which paragraph 490.05(1)(d) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(d) the condition set out in paragraph 490.029112(1)(b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` MEANS
    IF `(a) the person is subject to an order made under section 490.012 that applies for life under subsection 490.013(2.1), as it read from time to time before the day on which paragraph 490.05(1)(a) comes into force`
       OR (`(b) the person is subject to an obligation under section 490.019 that applies for life under paragraph 490.022(3)(d)` AND `(b) none of the offences listed in the notice in Form 53 served on the person in respect of the obligation have a maximum term of imprisonment for life`)
       OR (`(c) the person is subject to an obligation under section 490.02901 that applies for life under paragraph 490.02904(3)(d)` AND `(c) the obligation began before the day on which paragraph 490.05(1)(c) comes into force` AND `(c) the condition set out in paragraph 490.029051(1)(b) is met`)
       OR (`(d) the person is subject to an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act that applies for life under subsection 36.2(3) of that Act` AND `(d) the obligation began before the day on which paragraph 490.05(1)(d) comes into force` AND `(d) the condition set out in paragraph 490.029112(1)(b) is met`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may apply to a court for an order to vary the duration of" an order or obligation described in paragraphs (a) to (d)

-- src:10674 | Limitation
-- src:10675 | (2) A person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(c) or (d) if they have made an application for a variation order under section 490.029051 or 490.029112 in respect of the same obligation.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(2) (src:10674-10675)
GIVEN `the application is under paragraph (1)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have made an application for a variation order under section 490.029051 or 490.029112 in respect of the same obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.05(2) the person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(c) or (d)` MEANS
    IF `the application is under paragraph (1)(c) or (d)` AND `they have made an application for a variation order under section 490.029051 or 490.029112 in respect of the same obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(c) or (d) if they have made an application for a variation order"

-- src:10676 | Jurisdiction
-- src:10677 | (3) The application shall be made to
-- src:10678 | (a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, if the application is made under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of an order made by such a court; or
-- src:10679 | (b) a court of criminal jurisdiction, in any other case.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(3) (src:10676-10679)
DECLARE `s 490.05(3) court to which the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.05(3)(a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 490.05(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(3) (src:10676-10679)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 490.05(3) court to which the application is made`
`s 490.05(3) the court to which the application shall be made` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` AND `the application is in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    THEN `s 490.05(3)(a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    ELSE `s 490.05(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`   -- "(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction, in any other case"

-- src:10680 | Variation order
-- src:10681 | (4) The court shall make the variation order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the offences that are the basis of the order or obligation do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(4) (src:10680-10681)
DECLARE `s 490.05(4) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.05(4) make the variation order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(4) (src:10680-10681)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the offences that are the basis of the order or obligation do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.05(4) the court shall make the variation order` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the offences that are the basis of the order or obligation do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall make the variation order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the offences that are the basis of the order or obligation" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(4) (src:10680-10681)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.05(4) action`
`s 490.05(4) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.05(4) make the variation order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of the ground and did not make the variation order"

-- src:10682 | Variation of duration
-- src:10683 | (5) If the court makes a variation order, it shall set out the duration of the order or obligation in the order, which shall be determined by applying
-- src:10684 | (a) subsection 490.013(2) to the offence in question with the longest maximum term of imprisonment, in the case of an order under section 490.012;
-- src:10685 | (b) paragraphs 490.022(3)(a) and (b) to the offence in question with the longest maximum term of imprisonment, in the case of an obligation under section 490.019;
-- src:10686 | (c) paragraphs 490.02904(3)(a) and (b) to the offence in question whose equivalent offence has the longest maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law, in the case of an obligation under section 490.02901; and
-- src:10687 | (d) paragraphs 36.2(2)(a) and (b) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act to the offence in question whose equivalent criminal offence has the longest maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law, in the case of an obligation under section 36.1 of that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(5) (src:10682-10687)
DECLARE `s 490.05(5) kind of order or obligation` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.05(5)(a) an order under section 490.012`
    `s 490.05(5)(b) an obligation under section 490.019`
    `s 490.05(5)(c) an obligation under section 490.02901`
    `s 490.05(5)(d) an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(5) (src:10682-10687)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 490.05(5) kind of order or obligation`
      `the court makes a variation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence in question with the longest maximum term (for an obligation under section 490.02901, the maximum term provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence)` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for that offence` IS A DATE
      `the duration that subsection 490.013(2) gives for that offence, by s 490.013(2)` IS A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
      `the duration that paragraphs 36.2(2)(a) and (b) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act give for that offence, by section 36.2 of that Act` IS A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
`s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court makes a variation order`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court makes a variation order, it shall set out the duration"
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `s 490.05(5)(a) an order under section 490.012` THEN `the duration that subsection 490.013(2) gives for that offence, by s 490.013(2)`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection 490.013(2) is in another part
         WHEN `s 490.05(5)(d) an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` THEN `the duration that paragraphs 36.2(2)(a) and (b) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act give for that offence, by section 36.2 of that Act`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraphs 36.2(2)(a) and (b) are in another Act
         WHEN `s 490.05(5)(b) an obligation under section 490.019` THEN `the duration of paragraphs 490.022(3)(a) and (b)`
         WHEN `s 490.05(5)(c) an obligation under section 490.02901` THEN `the duration of paragraphs 490.022(3)(a) and (b)`   -- paragraphs 490.02904(3)(a) and (b) read the same way
    WHERE
        `the duration of paragraphs 490.022(3)(a) and (b)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 490.022(3) the band of the maximum term of imprisonment` `the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence in question with the longest maximum term (for an obligation under section 490.02901, the maximum term provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence)`
            WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for that offence` 10))
            WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for that offence` 20))
            WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of life` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only paragraphs (a) and (b) are to be applied
            WHEN `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names maximum terms of two, five, 10, 14 years and life only

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(5) (src:10682-10687)
DECLARE `s 490.05(5) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.05(5) set out the duration of the order or obligation in the variation order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(5) (src:10682-10687)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.05(5) action`
`s 490.05(5) the duty of the court to set out the duration` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.05(5) set out the duration of the order or obligation in the variation order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made a variation order and did not set out the duration of the order or obligation in it"

-- src:10688 | Reasons for decision
-- src:10689 | (6) The court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(6) (src:10688-10689)
DECLARE `s 490.05(6) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.05(6) give reasons for its decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(6) (src:10688-10689)
GIVEN `the court has made a decision under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.05(6) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a decision under this section` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "The court shall give reasons for its decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(6) (src:10688-10689)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.05(6) action`
`s 490.05(6) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.05(6) give reasons for its decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not give reasons for its decision"

-- src:10690 | Notification
-- src:10691 | (7) The court shall cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(7) (src:10690-10691)
DECLARE `s 490.05(7) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.05(7) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(7) (src:10690-10691)
GIVEN `the court makes a variation order under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.05(7) the court shall cause the notification to be given` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a variation order under this section` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "of a variation order made under this section"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.05(7) (src:10690-10691)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.05(7) action`
`s 490.05(7) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.05(7) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made a variation order and did not cause the notification to be given"

§ `490.06 Appeal`

-- src:10692 | Appeal
-- src:10693 | 490.06 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.04(4) or (5) or 490.05(4) or (5) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may
-- src:10694 | (a) dismiss the appeal; or
-- src:10695 | (b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made, as the case may be, under subsection 490.04(5) or section 490.05.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.06(1) (src:10692-10695)
DECLARE `s 490.06(1) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.06(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.06(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order`
    `s 490.06(1) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.06(1) (src:10692-10695)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.06(1) appellant`
      `the decision appealed from is a decision under subsection 490.04(4) or (5) or 490.05(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.06(1) the appeal may be brought` MEANS
    IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.06(1) another person` OR (NOT `the decision appealed from is a decision under subsection 490.04(4) or (5) or 490.05(4) or (5)`) OR (NOT `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.04(4) or (5) or 490.05(4) or (5) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10693 | 490.06 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.04(4) or (5) or 490.05(4) or (5) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may
-- src:10694 | (a) dismiss the appeal; or
-- src:10695 | (b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made, as the case may be, under subsection 490.04(5) or section 490.05.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.06(1) (src:10693-10695)
DECLARE `s 490.06(1) thing the appeal court does` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.06(1) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 490.06(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing`
    `s 490.06(1) quash the exemption order or variation order`
    `s 490.06(1) amend the exemption order or variation order`
    `s 490.06(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.04(5) or section 490.05`
    `s 490.06(1) another thing`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.06(1) (src:10693-10695)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 490.06(1) thing the appeal court does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.06(1) the appeal court may do it` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 490.06(1) dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.06(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.06(1) quash the exemption order or variation order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.06(1) amend the exemption order or variation order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.06(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.04(5) or section 490.05` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.06(1) another thing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made"

-- src:10696 | Removal of information from database
-- src:10697 | (2) If an appeal court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.06(2) (src:10696-10697)
DECLARE `s 490.06(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.06(2) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.06(2) (src:10696-10697)
GIVEN `an appeal court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.06(2) the appeal court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` MEANS
    IF `an appeal court makes an exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an appeal court makes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.06(2) (src:10696-10697)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.06(2) action`
`s 490.06(2) the duty of a court of appeal` MEANS
    PARTY `a court of appeal`
    MUST `s 490.06(2) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a court of appeal` BECAUSE "the appeal court made an exemption order and did not order the removal of the information"

§ `490.07 Requirements relating to notice`

-- src:10698 | Requirements relating to notice
-- src:10699 | 490.07 (1) If an appeal court quashes an exemption order, it shall cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision and shall cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.07(1) (src:10698-10699)
GIVEN `an appeal court quashes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.07(1) the appeal court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` MEANS
    IF `an appeal court quashes an exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an appeal court quashes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.07(1) (src:10698-10699)
DECLARE `s 490.07(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.07(1) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision`
    `s 490.07(1) cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.07(1) (src:10698-10699)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.07(1) action`
`s 490.07(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the Commissioner and the Attorney General to be notified` MEANS
    PARTY `a court of appeal`
    MUST `s 490.07(1) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a court of appeal` BECAUSE "the Commissioner and the Attorney General were not notified of the decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.07(1) (src:10698-10699)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.07(1) action`
`s 490.07(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the person to be informed of the sections` MEANS
    PARTY `a court of appeal`
    MUST `s 490.07(1) cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a court of appeal` BECAUSE "the person who applied was not informed of the sections"

